1
00:00:04,604 --> 00:00:05,839
Anterior resection of rectum.

2
00:00:05,905 --> 00:00:07,107
Monopolar.

3
00:00:13,346 --> 00:00:16,049
Fast. That's Dr. Daimon.

4
00:00:16,116 --> 00:00:18,351
To perform resection at this speed...

5
00:00:18,418 --> 00:00:19,586
No talking.

6
00:00:20,286 --> 00:00:22,555
First assistant,
pull the rectum to the ventral.

7
00:00:23,523 --> 00:00:24,357
You suck.

8
00:00:24,424 --> 00:00:26,426
Your countertraction is no good.

9
00:00:26,559 --> 00:00:29,629
The part-timer is so nice.

10
00:00:29,696 --> 00:00:31,398
This is the third surgery
without a break.

11
00:00:31,531 --> 00:00:34,634
Get ready for the next patient.
I'll keep on going.

12
00:00:35,268 --> 00:00:37,637
As usual, but no lunch break?

13
00:00:37,771 --> 00:00:39,072
My operations are quick.

14
00:00:39,205 --> 00:00:41,708
- Are you continuing?
- It's overwork.

15
00:00:41,775 --> 00:00:44,044
- Again. Wrong countertraction.
- Sorry.

16
00:00:44,110 --> 00:00:45,845
Power harassment and overwork.

17
00:00:46,546 --> 00:00:48,982
Someone will report her to the bureau.

18
00:00:49,249 --> 00:00:52,685
Maybe this is how she teaches.

19
00:00:55,422 --> 00:00:58,591
How long have you been a surgeon?
You're disqualified!

20
00:00:58,758 --> 00:01:00,560
- Switch the first assistant!
- Yes.

21
00:01:00,760 --> 00:01:01,661
Tweezers.

22
00:01:03,696 --> 00:01:04,864
Ventral.

23
00:01:04,931 --> 00:01:06,766
His heart is broken to pieces.

24
00:01:08,701 --> 00:01:11,404
What a wonderful education.

25
00:01:11,771 --> 00:01:12,639
Good.

26
00:01:13,807 --> 00:01:15,542
SURGERY DEPARTMENT OFFICE

27
00:01:17,777 --> 00:01:21,114
I want to use gene therapy data
for my papers.

28
00:01:21,214 --> 00:01:23,116
Pick out relevant documents.

29
00:01:23,349 --> 00:01:24,350
Pardon?

30
00:01:24,417 --> 00:01:25,385
This much?

31
00:01:25,819 --> 00:01:28,655
This is one of the important
tasks of a doctor.

32
00:01:28,855 --> 00:01:31,224
Get some help then.

33
00:01:33,460 --> 00:01:35,728
What? Are you going to help?

34
00:01:35,795 --> 00:01:38,565
I decline work
that doesn't require a medical license.

35
00:01:38,631 --> 00:01:40,233
It's 5 PM. I'm going home.

36
00:01:40,533 --> 00:01:44,237
- I'll go home.
- Me, too.

37
00:01:45,004 --> 00:01:49,008
You should ask
if there's anything you can do.

38
00:01:49,075 --> 00:01:50,276
The professors are still here.

39
00:01:50,410 --> 00:01:55,181
But wasn't there an overwork warning
from the bureau?

40
00:01:55,248 --> 00:01:57,750
Goodbye...

41
00:01:57,884 --> 00:01:59,686
Goodbye...

42
00:02:02,122 --> 00:02:04,057
The youngsters now are hard to understand.

43
00:02:04,324 --> 00:02:06,759
They refuse go out for drinks
and don't work overtime.

44
00:02:06,993 --> 00:02:09,262
They prefer video games over girls.

45
00:02:09,329 --> 00:02:10,830
They have no desire to marry.

46
00:02:12,198 --> 00:02:13,199
How about you?

47
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:16,069
What? That's abrupt.

48
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:21,374
How about something like this?

49
00:02:21,841 --> 00:02:22,909
Matchmaking party?

50
00:02:23,042 --> 00:02:25,345
It's time I get serious about
getting married.

51
00:02:25,478 --> 00:02:26,613
Do you want to join me?

52
00:02:27,614 --> 00:02:30,016
MATCHMAKING PARTY VENUE

53
00:02:36,823 --> 00:02:40,026
- I'm glad you met a nice girl.
- Thank you.

54
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:42,996
It's amazing I met such a wonderful girl.

55
00:02:43,663 --> 00:02:45,031
Lucky...

56
00:02:45,465 --> 00:02:46,766
- Here.
- For me?

57
00:02:54,574 --> 00:02:57,544
I wouldn't have minded
if you went for a drink with her.

58
00:02:57,777 --> 00:02:58,811
But...

59
00:02:59,279 --> 00:03:00,813
Go ahead and marry her.

60
00:03:01,314 --> 00:03:05,451
Young people say marriage isn't
cost-efficient.

61
00:03:06,619 --> 00:03:10,924
If you don't have the stability of
a family you can't do this job.

62
00:03:10,990 --> 00:03:12,892
- I can't stand it.
- Right?

63
00:03:14,394 --> 00:03:20,033
I'm having a hard time communicating
with this pressure-free generation.

64
00:03:20,099 --> 00:03:23,336
Our boss don't get along
and I'm forced to do their work.

65
00:03:23,403 --> 00:03:24,804
I know.

66
00:03:24,938 --> 00:03:26,306
It's okay, I ordered a drink.

67
00:03:26,940 --> 00:03:30,777
Each one of the three bosses
thinks he's the best.

68
00:03:32,312 --> 00:03:34,581
They're always saying
"yes sir."

69
00:03:34,781 --> 00:03:36,282
Are they bureaucrats?!

70
00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:41,354
If this is to go on,

71
00:03:42,622 --> 00:03:44,757
I won't be able to...

72
00:03:46,492 --> 00:03:51,564
care for my patients' feelings
because my own heart will break.

73
00:03:52,632 --> 00:03:58,504
Today I'm only having super deluxe.
Keep them coming!

74
00:03:58,638 --> 00:04:04,577
Squid tentacles, sea grapes,
and skate wings. All super deluxe!

75
00:04:04,744 --> 00:04:06,746
You deserve it.

76
00:04:06,879 --> 00:04:09,482
You've earned much money
from the 10 operations.

77
00:04:11,484 --> 00:04:14,053
Another jug.

78
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:16,990
Here you are.

79
00:04:17,957 --> 00:04:20,827
Yeah!

80
00:04:20,960 --> 00:04:21,894
Freedom.

81
00:04:22,862 --> 00:04:24,564
Don't imitate her.

82
00:04:25,265 --> 00:04:27,100
Your heart will break.

83
00:04:27,166 --> 00:04:31,804
Keep drinking! Keep doing operations!
Just keep doing.

84
00:04:36,276 --> 00:04:40,046
This is the story of
a lone wolf woman doctor.

85
00:04:40,546 --> 00:04:45,285
Inomata's case attracted
the attention of media.

86
00:04:47,687 --> 00:04:52,558
Daimon was involved in this case,
wasn't she?

87
00:04:53,426 --> 00:04:59,565
She is a raging horse.
She has no place among our thoroughbreds.

88
00:05:00,533 --> 00:05:01,467
Yes, I know.

89
00:05:02,068 --> 00:05:03,569
How's your wife?

90
00:05:03,636 --> 00:05:05,338
Yes. Well...

91
00:05:06,205 --> 00:05:11,811
She is very happy to be back in Tokyo.

92
00:05:11,911 --> 00:05:12,812
Thank you so much.

93
00:05:14,047 --> 00:05:17,150
Take care of your family.
Even if it's just for face value.

94
00:05:18,418 --> 00:05:23,256
I've divorced twice
and have awkward family relationships.

95
00:05:25,091 --> 00:05:27,760
I'll take good care of my family, sir.

96
00:05:29,696 --> 00:05:31,230
But Chairman,

97
00:05:31,364 --> 00:05:37,136
why are you so young and energetic?
I envy you.

98
00:05:40,073 --> 00:05:41,441
<i>In 2017</i>

99
00:05:41,708 --> 00:05:46,212
<i>the university medical system</i>
<i>regained its once-lost authority</i>

100
00:05:46,779 --> 00:05:52,485
<i>and the system on which lives depend</i>
<i>strayed away from what it should be.</i>

101
00:05:52,819 --> 00:05:54,987
Thank you for waiting.

102
00:05:55,054 --> 00:06:01,694
Chairman Uchikanda is
giving special attention to us.

103
00:06:02,195 --> 00:06:07,567
So please avoid complacency.

104
00:06:07,734 --> 00:06:08,735
Yes sir...

105
00:06:09,235 --> 00:06:11,104
Good. Thumbs up.

106
00:06:11,604 --> 00:06:12,438
Let's go.

107
00:06:13,773 --> 00:06:16,342
Chairman Uchikanda.

108
00:06:16,676 --> 00:06:17,510
What's wrong?

109
00:06:18,277 --> 00:06:19,812
Nothing.

110
00:06:20,313 --> 00:06:25,151
By the way,
how's your girl from the party?

111
00:06:26,085 --> 00:06:28,287
Yes, she's okay.

112
00:06:28,354 --> 00:06:30,456
Okay? Did you propose to her?

113
00:06:32,725 --> 00:06:35,027
- What?
- Huh?

114
00:06:35,128 --> 00:06:37,163
- You panicked.
- What?

115
00:06:48,841 --> 00:06:49,742
Excuse me,

116
00:06:50,109 --> 00:06:52,278
where is the Surgery Department Office?

117
00:06:52,945 --> 00:06:54,046
Shiori!

118
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:56,182
Shiori! Shiori.

119
00:06:57,116 --> 00:06:59,585
- I'm sorry.
- Excuse me.

120
00:06:59,819 --> 00:07:01,621
Why are you here?

121
00:07:01,821 --> 00:07:03,956
- Sorry to bother you.
- It's okay.

122
00:07:04,023 --> 00:07:07,160
Actually I made a reservation.

123
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:10,029
Really? That place?

124
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:16,502
But it's very popular.
It's still one year away.

125
00:07:16,736 --> 00:07:19,439
No problem.

126
00:07:19,939 --> 00:07:20,773
It's good.

127
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:23,943
- You really liked the place.
- Thank you.

128
00:07:24,010 --> 00:07:25,578
- Good.
- Yes.

129
00:07:27,246 --> 00:07:31,684
<i>In the midst of this, doctors free</i>
<i>from any establishment emerged.</i>

130
00:07:31,951 --> 00:07:35,555
<i>Freelance doctors, in other words,</i>
<i>lone wolf doctors.</i>

131
00:07:35,755 --> 00:07:37,690
Good morning, Dr. Daimon.

132
00:07:38,458 --> 00:07:39,492
- Oh.
- Hi.

133
00:07:40,593 --> 00:07:42,395
Well, see you...

134
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:46,599
Can I call you tonight?

135
00:07:46,766 --> 00:07:49,135
- Of course.
- Good.

136
00:07:49,735 --> 00:07:51,370
- Bye.
- Bye.

137
00:08:02,882 --> 00:08:03,716
Shiori!

138
00:08:03,950 --> 00:08:04,951
Are you all right?

139
00:08:05,251 --> 00:08:06,118
Shiori.

140
00:08:07,153 --> 00:08:08,020
Hey...

141
00:08:08,087 --> 00:08:10,156
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

142
00:08:10,423 --> 00:08:14,460
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

143
00:08:14,760 --> 00:08:19,699
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>
<i>and the skills she has acquired.</i>

144
00:08:20,766 --> 00:08:22,602
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

145
00:08:23,469 --> 00:08:24,604
<i>Also known as...</i>

146
00:08:25,071 --> 00:08:26,939
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

147
00:08:47,793 --> 00:08:48,995
Liver cancer.

148
00:08:49,896 --> 00:08:52,865
A huge 10 cm tumor centering around
the right lobe of liver.

149
00:08:53,032 --> 00:08:55,101
Multiple tumors also found in
the left lobe of liver.

150
00:08:55,701 --> 00:08:57,470
An advanced case.

151
00:08:57,537 --> 00:08:59,906
I'm amazed she didn't notice symptoms.

152
00:09:00,039 --> 00:09:02,775
The patient is
Morimoto's girlfriend.

153
00:09:02,842 --> 00:09:04,143
Really?

154
00:09:04,277 --> 00:09:07,413
It's even infiltrated into
the inferior vena cava.

155
00:09:07,680 --> 00:09:10,750
If nothing is done,
she'll die in three months.

156
00:09:10,917 --> 00:09:13,419
You're insensitive, Dr. Daimon.

157
00:09:13,586 --> 00:09:16,155
Why? Let's just cure her.

158
00:09:16,422 --> 00:09:18,257
But it's not an easy surgery.

159
00:09:18,324 --> 00:09:20,226
With the tumor spread out like this,

160
00:09:20,293 --> 00:09:23,796
I'm not sure we can leave more than
20% of the liver.

161
00:09:24,130 --> 00:09:27,366
That's the least amount needed
to regenerate itself.

162
00:09:27,633 --> 00:09:31,504
I'll go talk to her.

163
00:09:36,108 --> 00:09:38,210
Troublesome tumor.

164
00:09:40,546 --> 00:09:43,482
But Dr. Ebina, you don't have to stare.

165
00:09:44,450 --> 00:09:46,452
SHIORI UCHIKANDA

166
00:09:47,119 --> 00:09:48,154
Uchikanda?

167
00:09:49,021 --> 00:09:49,855
What?

168
00:09:51,757 --> 00:09:52,592
Liver cancer?

169
00:09:53,259 --> 00:09:56,162
You'll have surgery soon.

170
00:09:57,496 --> 00:10:00,199
Don't worry. This hospital is
one of the best in Japan.

171
00:10:00,266 --> 00:10:01,801
You'll be better after surgery.

172
00:10:03,836 --> 00:10:04,670
Excuse me.

173
00:10:04,971 --> 00:10:08,774
Nice to meet you.
I'm Dr. Ebina.

174
00:10:10,409 --> 00:10:12,078
Nice to meet you, too.

175
00:10:12,345 --> 00:10:17,350
Uchikanda is a rare surname.

176
00:10:18,017 --> 00:10:20,953
Japan Doctors Club's Chairman's
surname is also Uchikanda.

177
00:10:21,220 --> 00:10:22,188
This is...

178
00:10:23,222 --> 00:10:24,423
a coincidence, right?

179
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:29,328
Coincidence?

180
00:10:33,399 --> 00:10:35,334
Kagenobu Uchikanda is

181
00:10:36,869 --> 00:10:38,237
my father.

182
00:10:40,673 --> 00:10:44,243
But my parents are divorced.

183
00:10:44,343 --> 00:10:46,812
I picked my father's surname.

184
00:10:47,346 --> 00:10:48,347
I see.

185
00:10:48,948 --> 00:10:50,516
What can I say?

186
00:10:51,083 --> 00:10:52,752
He didn't tell me anything.

187
00:10:53,552 --> 00:10:58,424
I asked him to keep it a secret.

188
00:10:59,191 --> 00:11:01,527
Because my father has a new family.

189
00:11:01,827 --> 00:11:06,465
If he knew of my illness,
it would bother him.

190
00:11:07,066 --> 00:11:07,933
So...

191
00:11:09,769 --> 00:11:12,672
please keep it to yourself.

192
00:11:13,406 --> 00:11:17,176
Don't worry.
I'll prepare a special room for you.

193
00:11:17,877 --> 00:11:24,383
Once again my name is
Takashi Ebina.

194
00:11:24,850 --> 00:11:27,253
Please say hello to him for me.

195
00:11:28,254 --> 00:11:29,555
- Dr. Ebina.
- What?

196
00:11:29,822 --> 00:11:31,991
- Please, don't.
- I won't tell anyone.

197
00:11:33,893 --> 00:11:35,928
- Chairman Uchikanda's daughter?
- Yes.

198
00:11:36,162 --> 00:11:39,865
Hepatoma stage 4A. She needs to
have surgery ASAP.

199
00:11:40,866 --> 00:11:42,601
I can't believe it.

200
00:11:42,668 --> 00:11:46,972
Morimoto is dating the daughter of
Chairman Uchikanda.

201
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:48,874
He's been hiding it from us.

202
00:11:49,008 --> 00:11:51,811
I think you'd better
tell Chairman Uchikanda.

203
00:11:51,944 --> 00:11:54,313
I don't think so.

204
00:11:54,513 --> 00:11:57,516
Because his daughter said
to keep it a secret, right?

205
00:11:57,650 --> 00:11:58,984
But this is a serious matter.

206
00:11:59,485 --> 00:12:01,420
If she loses her life here...

207
00:12:01,554 --> 00:12:04,523
Why are you saying
such a horrible thing?

208
00:12:04,590 --> 00:12:05,491
Sorry.

209
00:12:05,891 --> 00:12:09,428
Conversely it can be a chance.

210
00:12:09,495 --> 00:12:13,799
If we can cure her,
he'll owe us much.

211
00:12:14,133 --> 00:12:15,501
You're right.

212
00:12:15,634 --> 00:12:18,370
Please let me be her surgeon.

213
00:12:19,905 --> 00:12:23,743
Let's do our best to save her life.

214
00:12:23,809 --> 00:12:27,379
I'm the right candidate for this case.

215
00:12:27,513 --> 00:12:29,014
I'll be happy to perform the surgery.

216
00:12:29,148 --> 00:12:31,484
The next chief surgeon
should do it...

217
00:12:31,617 --> 00:12:34,253
Hey, wait a minute.

218
00:12:35,521 --> 00:12:36,388
Well...

219
00:12:37,256 --> 00:12:40,926
This patient is very important.

220
00:12:41,460 --> 00:12:42,795
So make sure nothing happens.

221
00:12:43,262 --> 00:12:46,298
Torii, Inomata, Ebina.

222
00:12:46,766 --> 00:12:50,803
Why don't you three become a team?

223
00:12:51,704 --> 00:12:53,639
- What?
- A dream team of doctors

224
00:12:53,706 --> 00:12:56,108
by the three Takashis.
The team is formed!

225
00:12:57,143 --> 00:12:59,879
- Congratulations.
- Thank you...

226
00:13:00,012 --> 00:13:02,047
SPECIAL ROOM B

227
00:13:02,114 --> 00:13:03,215
Excuse me.

228
00:13:03,783 --> 00:13:05,251
This is Dr. Daimon.

229
00:13:05,851 --> 00:13:10,322
I heard you're a very brilliant doctor.

230
00:13:10,389 --> 00:13:11,223
By the way,

231
00:13:11,524 --> 00:13:14,093
advanced hepatoma has spread to
the blood vessel.

232
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:15,895
You'll have surgery immediately.

233
00:13:18,931 --> 00:13:19,765
Will I...

234
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:21,967
survive?

235
00:13:22,501 --> 00:13:25,671
Yes. If you have surgery.
Let me cut it.

236
00:13:25,805 --> 00:13:27,573
Don't be selfish.

237
00:13:28,007 --> 00:13:30,910
Daimon, keep away from her.

238
00:13:30,976 --> 00:13:32,545
Why?

239
00:13:32,745 --> 00:13:34,046
Nice to
meet you.

240
00:13:34,547 --> 00:13:38,617
I'm the next chief surgeon, Inomata.

241
00:13:39,351 --> 00:13:42,087
I'm the next chief surgeon, Torii.

242
00:13:42,321 --> 00:13:45,624
Us, the professors' team
will be in charge of your surgery.

243
00:13:45,691 --> 00:13:47,593
Once again, I'm Ebina.

244
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:50,863
Thank you, but...

245
00:13:52,464 --> 00:13:53,365
I prefer...

246
00:13:55,301 --> 00:13:59,004
Dr. Morimoto for my surgery.

247
00:13:59,839 --> 00:14:01,507
- Morimoto?
- You're going to die.

248
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:02,575
Excuse me?

249
00:14:02,708 --> 00:14:06,011
This surgery isn't easy.

250
00:14:06,846 --> 00:14:09,949
I think Morimoto
lacks experience.

251
00:14:10,015 --> 00:14:11,217
No, he is fine.

252
00:14:11,584 --> 00:14:15,521
He isn't like a typical doctor
at university hospitals.

253
00:14:16,188 --> 00:14:18,791
He has more than just a medical license.

254
00:14:20,492 --> 00:14:22,328
He graduated from a medical
university in Cuba.

255
00:14:22,728 --> 00:14:26,832
He's also licensed as a vet,
a ship surgeon and a military surgeon.

256
00:14:26,899 --> 00:14:28,634
Shiori, wait.

257
00:14:28,701 --> 00:14:32,504
Moreover his special skills and hobby
are both surgery.

258
00:14:32,771 --> 00:14:36,976
Is there such a wonderful doctor?

259
00:14:38,043 --> 00:14:38,878
Wow.

260
00:14:39,845 --> 00:14:41,213
No. Well...

261
00:14:41,347 --> 00:14:42,915
- Dr. Morimoto.
- Yes.

262
00:14:44,416 --> 00:14:45,251
I won't...

263
00:14:47,052 --> 00:14:49,121
have surgery if the surgeon...

264
00:14:51,156 --> 00:14:52,291
is not Dr. Morimoto.

265
00:14:59,498 --> 00:15:01,300
I can't believe
how pretentious you are.

266
00:15:02,067 --> 00:15:05,271
- Aren't you ashamed?
- I'm sorry.

267
00:15:05,537 --> 00:15:08,374
You pretend like you are not
interested in a promotion.

268
00:15:08,874 --> 00:15:11,677
You're trying to curry favor
with Chairman Uchikanda.

269
00:15:11,744 --> 00:15:14,813
No, I'm not.
I don't care whose daughter she is.

270
00:15:15,147 --> 00:15:18,817
She doesn't like people to look at
her like that, so it was a secret.

271
00:15:19,251 --> 00:15:20,352
Liar! Hypocrite!

272
00:15:20,486 --> 00:15:23,222
Told a pack of lies and got her!

273
00:15:23,289 --> 00:15:24,490
Such an imposter!

274
00:15:24,790 --> 00:15:26,125
When did you go to Cuba?

275
00:15:26,258 --> 00:15:29,128
Show me your veterinary license.
You said you're scared of dogs!

276
00:15:29,228 --> 00:15:31,630
I invited you but
you tried to outwit me. Traitor!

277
00:15:31,964 --> 00:15:34,633
Dr. Daimon, we'll sue him for fraud.

278
00:15:34,700 --> 00:15:36,035
Kin. Shut up.

279
00:15:36,936 --> 00:15:39,805
I'm not Kin. I'm Mamoru Hara.

280
00:15:39,872 --> 00:15:41,740
Morimoto, decline the surgery.

281
00:15:42,174 --> 00:15:45,311
You know you can't handle
the operation.

282
00:15:48,380 --> 00:15:49,248
Morimoto,

283
00:15:50,716 --> 00:15:52,284
I understand how you feel.

284
00:15:52,418 --> 00:15:55,354
If there's anything I can do for you,
let me know.

285
00:15:55,587 --> 00:15:57,256
Thank you.

286
00:15:57,323 --> 00:15:59,892
Actually I had the same case before.

287
00:16:00,392 --> 00:16:04,196
You can recommend me to her.

288
00:16:04,730 --> 00:16:06,131
Was your surgery successful?

289
00:16:14,606 --> 00:16:16,308
See? Casey.

290
00:16:16,508 --> 00:16:19,211
Chairman Uchikanda's daughter.

291
00:16:19,278 --> 00:16:21,113
That's too bad.

292
00:16:21,180 --> 00:16:23,248
He's divorced?

293
00:16:23,349 --> 00:16:26,051
Yes, twice. He's with his third wife now.

294
00:16:26,385 --> 00:16:28,587
I'm not sure how many children
he has.

295
00:16:29,188 --> 00:16:33,192
He's popular with the ladies.
He looks like it.

296
00:16:33,425 --> 00:16:34,293
Really?

297
00:16:34,426 --> 00:16:37,830
If Dr. Morimoto marries her,

298
00:16:37,963 --> 00:16:40,432
he'll be promoted at once.

299
00:16:40,632 --> 00:16:42,568
That Dr. Morimoto.

300
00:16:42,701 --> 00:16:44,970
By the way,
she has a troublesome tumor.

301
00:16:45,204 --> 00:16:47,539
Excision will result in
low residual liver volume.

302
00:16:47,673 --> 00:16:50,876
It's hard for Dr. Morimoto.

303
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:54,046
He never grows up.

304
00:16:54,780 --> 00:16:56,348
Dr. Daimon. Let him be your disciple.

305
00:16:56,782 --> 00:16:57,683
I decline.

306
00:16:57,950 --> 00:16:59,885
She's not fit to be a teacher.

307
00:17:00,119 --> 00:17:03,022
But training a surgeon is important.

308
00:17:03,255 --> 00:17:07,659
If we have more good doctors,
we can save more patients.

309
00:17:08,994 --> 00:17:11,497
Training, huh.

310
00:17:14,900 --> 00:17:18,270
My hand has also grown well.

311
00:17:19,538 --> 00:17:22,608
"Menchin." "Baiman."

312
00:17:23,742 --> 00:17:25,978
You helped it grow!

313
00:17:29,515 --> 00:17:34,553
The patient still wants Morimoto
to do her surgery?

314
00:17:34,686 --> 00:17:36,688
Yes, I tried to persuade her
but she insists.

315
00:17:37,322 --> 00:17:41,427
I may be asking you too much

316
00:17:41,593 --> 00:17:44,496
but can you three be his assistants?

317
00:17:44,696 --> 00:17:45,864
- Assistants?
- Yeah.

318
00:17:47,099 --> 00:17:48,967
With all due respect Director,

319
00:17:49,401 --> 00:17:51,236
if I'm his assistant,

320
00:17:51,970 --> 00:17:54,473
it'll be difficult for him.

321
00:17:54,540 --> 00:17:56,708
I'm not good at surgery.

322
00:17:56,909 --> 00:17:58,143
So what?

323
00:17:58,710 --> 00:18:00,379
What should we do?

324
00:18:00,979 --> 00:18:05,751
If we fail her operation,
everyone gets fired.

325
00:18:06,351 --> 00:18:07,786
- Director.
- What?

326
00:18:09,054 --> 00:18:11,657
Can Dr. Daimon be my assistant?

327
00:18:11,857 --> 00:18:13,225
- Daimon?
- Yes.

328
00:18:13,659 --> 00:18:14,760
Oh, okay.

329
00:18:15,527 --> 00:18:16,595
That's the only choice.

330
00:18:16,728 --> 00:18:20,766
But I don't think
she will accept the position.

331
00:18:20,899 --> 00:18:22,701
It's impossible to persuade her.

332
00:18:22,835 --> 00:18:26,205
She'll say
"I decline to be an assistant."

333
00:18:26,271 --> 00:18:28,874
You don't like this and that!

334
00:18:29,074 --> 00:18:30,542
You're acting like a little kid!

335
00:18:30,976 --> 00:18:33,145
If we fail this operation,

336
00:18:34,279 --> 00:18:35,914
it's gonna be a disaster!

337
00:18:36,348 --> 00:18:42,020
I want you to ask her with
your knees on the ground.

338
00:18:42,454 --> 00:18:43,889
Just go!

339
00:18:44,490 --> 00:18:45,324
Oh come on.

340
00:18:46,992 --> 00:18:48,327
I decline to be an assistant.

341
00:18:49,027 --> 00:18:52,965
Look at us.
Don't you feel anything?

342
00:18:53,031 --> 00:18:55,134
- I'll operate.
- We can't ignore

343
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:56,802
the Chairman's daughter.

344
00:18:56,869 --> 00:18:58,737
I'm not interested in who she is.

345
00:18:58,804 --> 00:19:00,005
Daimon, please.

346
00:19:01,140 --> 00:19:04,309
Please support Morimoto.

347
00:19:04,376 --> 00:19:05,777
So I decline.

348
00:19:06,345 --> 00:19:09,214
Decline, decline.
Who do you think you are?!

349
00:19:09,982 --> 00:19:12,818
You don't want to guide and
train our staff?

350
00:19:12,885 --> 00:19:14,653
Does it require a medical license?

351
00:19:15,487 --> 00:19:16,321
Yes, you do!

352
00:19:17,222 --> 00:19:18,891
Either way I decline.

353
00:19:21,627 --> 00:19:22,628
I'm off to lunch.

354
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:36,842
Dr. Daimon, please.

355
00:19:37,910 --> 00:19:40,746
I don't mind if you operate.

356
00:19:41,480 --> 00:19:44,917
But don't tell Shiori.

357
00:19:48,120 --> 00:19:49,388
Please, help me.

358
00:19:49,922 --> 00:19:51,523
I want to save Shiori.

359
00:19:51,790 --> 00:19:53,458
Why don't you do it yourself?

360
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:57,996
I know about myself.

361
00:19:58,864 --> 00:20:00,632
My skill is third-rate anyway.

362
00:20:02,534 --> 00:20:07,139
I decided to see patients as a person,
not just as a case of illness.

363
00:20:07,372 --> 00:20:10,876
This way I can be competent,
though not like you.

364
00:20:11,376 --> 00:20:13,045
I don't get it.

365
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:16,448
You're so hands off.

366
00:20:17,015 --> 00:20:20,252
If you have time to complain,
get ready for the operation.

367
00:20:24,323 --> 00:20:26,525
Not see the case but the patient?

368
00:20:27,059 --> 00:20:31,263
They come here for cure.

369
00:20:34,766 --> 00:20:38,637
You don't understand because
you've never failed!

370
00:21:05,030 --> 00:21:05,897
Shiori.

371
00:21:07,332 --> 00:21:08,267
Are you all right?

372
00:21:12,371 --> 00:21:13,739
You'll never know

373
00:21:14,973 --> 00:21:17,576
what's going to happen.

374
00:21:19,811 --> 00:21:25,150
I never thought
it would come to this.

375
00:21:26,151 --> 00:21:26,985
Shiori.

376
00:21:28,220 --> 00:21:29,054
If...

377
00:21:31,723 --> 00:21:33,892
my surgery is successful,

378
00:21:36,228 --> 00:21:38,530
I will do it right.

379
00:21:39,598 --> 00:21:40,432
Yes.

380
00:21:42,934 --> 00:21:43,769
But...

381
00:21:46,405 --> 00:21:48,807
I'm scared.

382
00:21:50,575 --> 00:21:51,743
I think

383
00:21:52,177 --> 00:21:56,948
maybe I'll only have
a bit more time to talk to you.

384
00:22:02,087 --> 00:22:06,425
They come here for cure.

385
00:22:13,732 --> 00:22:14,566
Shiori.

386
00:22:15,467 --> 00:22:16,802
Believe in me.

387
00:22:18,070 --> 00:22:21,306
I'll save your life.

388
00:22:32,451 --> 00:22:36,054
I would never dare to do
my girlfriend's surgery.

389
00:22:36,121 --> 00:22:39,658
She is the chairman's daughter, right?

390
00:22:40,125 --> 00:22:42,394
I'll be too scared to do such surgery.

391
00:22:46,198 --> 00:22:47,165
Good.

392
00:22:47,232 --> 00:22:50,936
Goodbye...

393
00:22:53,939 --> 00:22:54,773
Here.

394
00:22:56,208 --> 00:22:57,642
I'm sorry about the other day.

395
00:22:59,444 --> 00:23:00,278
Anything?

396
00:23:00,946 --> 00:23:03,448
I must do it myself.
I'm the only person.

397
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:09,654
I'll be your assistant.

398
00:23:11,556 --> 00:23:14,292
It would be all right
if the two of us work together.

399
00:23:14,559 --> 00:23:15,427
Do our best.

400
00:23:16,027 --> 00:23:17,496
- Thank you.
- No problem.

401
00:23:24,936 --> 00:23:26,571
Dr. Daimon. It's unusual.

402
00:23:26,905 --> 00:23:28,306
It's already past 5 PM.

403
00:23:40,919 --> 00:23:43,321
After all, she cares about us.

404
00:23:47,926 --> 00:23:48,894
Dr. Daimon.

405
00:23:53,298 --> 00:23:56,535
Are you sure we can leave it
to Dr. Morimoto?

406
00:23:58,270 --> 00:24:02,774
Unless he excises very accurately
he can't keep 20% of the liver.

407
00:24:04,443 --> 00:24:05,410
I know.

408
00:24:08,747 --> 00:24:10,115
I'll be his assistant, too.

409
00:24:12,083 --> 00:24:14,986
Do you have a plan B?

410
00:24:15,754 --> 00:24:17,155
It'll end up in failure.

411
00:24:18,123 --> 00:24:19,090
Bye.

412
00:24:33,238 --> 00:24:35,974
This is the chairman's
daughter's operation.

413
00:24:36,041 --> 00:24:37,509
Are you sure this is all right?

414
00:24:38,543 --> 00:24:41,379
If you're worried,
why don't you help them.

415
00:24:47,586 --> 00:24:50,655
Don't look at his eyes.
We'll get involved.

416
00:24:57,829 --> 00:24:58,964
We'll begin.

417
00:24:59,397 --> 00:25:01,967
Right hepatic trisegmentectomy and

418
00:25:02,868 --> 00:25:06,204
caudate lobe resection and
the lateral segmental partial resection.

419
00:25:07,205 --> 00:25:11,343
Vitals. BP 103 over 75.
Pulse 64, normal sinus rhythm.

420
00:25:13,245 --> 00:25:14,079
Scalpel.

421
00:25:32,397 --> 00:25:33,598
Dr. Daimon.

422
00:25:34,099 --> 00:25:35,867
Switch assistant.
I'm your first assistant.

423
00:25:35,934 --> 00:25:36,768
Yes.

424
00:25:37,669 --> 00:25:40,238
Dr. Daimon.

425
00:25:40,639 --> 00:25:42,707
Thank you for coming.

426
00:25:43,909 --> 00:25:46,011
I'm seeing you in a new light.

427
00:25:46,278 --> 00:25:47,112
Let's do it.

428
00:25:47,812 --> 00:25:48,847
Yes!

429
00:25:50,181 --> 00:25:55,287
I see. She knew he couldn't so
she'll take his place.

430
00:25:55,687 --> 00:25:57,956
After all, it's "I'll cut it" again.

431
00:25:58,089 --> 00:25:59,758
But better than fail.

432
00:26:00,191 --> 00:26:02,561
First priority is to save her life.

433
00:26:03,662 --> 00:26:05,063
Mercedes incision.

434
00:26:07,198 --> 00:26:08,633
Get ready for wound retractor.

435
00:26:29,654 --> 00:26:31,523
Lateral growth of tumor.

436
00:26:35,794 --> 00:26:37,362
Too bad...

437
00:26:37,495 --> 00:26:40,865
In this condition,
radical resection is impossible.

438
00:26:45,136 --> 00:26:47,572
Lateral segmental partial resection.

439
00:26:47,739 --> 00:26:50,241
Starting with S2 partial resection.

440
00:26:50,809 --> 00:26:51,743
Monopolar.

441
00:27:01,653 --> 00:27:02,621
Sweat.

442
00:27:02,687 --> 00:27:04,122
Yes.

443
00:27:09,327 --> 00:27:12,664
SURGERY TIME

444
00:27:16,935 --> 00:27:18,103
Sorry. Sweat.

445
00:27:18,169 --> 00:27:19,504
Yes.

446
00:27:36,254 --> 00:27:38,690
Completion of S2 tumorectomy.

447
00:27:39,457 --> 00:27:41,192
Next, S3 partial resection.

448
00:27:42,260 --> 00:27:43,094
Monopolar.

449
00:27:44,229 --> 00:27:45,096
Morimoto.

450
00:27:46,131 --> 00:27:50,301
Get closer. You need to leave
more than 20% of the liver.

451
00:27:50,735 --> 00:27:52,137
Yes, I know.

452
00:27:55,140 --> 00:27:56,474
This is the limit.

453
00:27:59,444 --> 00:28:03,481
Morimoto, good job.
Daimon will take over.

454
00:28:11,756 --> 00:28:13,658
Daimon, you're in charge.

455
00:28:15,326 --> 00:28:16,795
- I decline.
- What?

456
00:28:18,029 --> 00:28:19,264
Decline?

457
00:28:19,497 --> 00:28:22,267
What do you mean decline?

458
00:28:22,834 --> 00:28:24,836
- Take over.
- I'm his assistant.

459
00:28:25,070 --> 00:28:25,937
Don't play
games!

460
00:28:26,471 --> 00:28:27,706
You know we can't fail this surgery.

461
00:28:33,044 --> 00:28:33,945
Nothing?

462
00:28:34,713 --> 00:28:36,648
What are you thinking?

463
00:28:36,781 --> 00:28:38,583
Surgeon, what's next?

464
00:28:41,753 --> 00:28:43,088
Ultrasonic scalpel.

465
00:28:49,027 --> 00:28:50,795
It's reckless. Stop it!

466
00:28:51,229 --> 00:28:53,698
That part-timer. What's she thinking?

467
00:28:54,432 --> 00:28:58,670
Maybe Daimon is training him?

468
00:28:59,471 --> 00:29:00,338
Train him?

469
00:29:01,106 --> 00:29:02,107
That Daimon?

470
00:29:02,841 --> 00:29:04,175
That stupid woman.

471
00:29:04,375 --> 00:29:06,978
Of all the operations,
why's she acting like that.

472
00:29:10,782 --> 00:29:12,717
Completion of S3 tumorectomy.

473
00:29:15,653 --> 00:29:16,621
Dr. Daimon,

474
00:29:17,422 --> 00:29:20,125
I can't go on.

475
00:29:20,992 --> 00:29:21,826
Take my place.

476
00:29:23,294 --> 00:29:25,063
To save her life. Please.

477
00:29:25,263 --> 00:29:27,432
Hey, Daimon. Switch!

478
00:29:27,866 --> 00:29:28,767
I decline.

479
00:29:29,501 --> 00:29:30,435
There she goes.

480
00:29:30,502 --> 00:29:31,469
Why?

481
00:29:31,603 --> 00:29:33,338
Surgeon, what's next?

482
00:29:36,808 --> 00:29:38,109
If we continue,

483
00:29:38,543 --> 00:29:42,580
the liver will be below 20%,
causing liver insufficiency.

484
00:29:43,047 --> 00:29:44,015
So?

485
00:29:44,682 --> 00:29:45,550
So...

486
00:29:47,952 --> 00:29:49,287
This condition is inoperable.

487
00:29:49,521 --> 00:29:50,822
Inoperable!

488
00:29:50,889 --> 00:29:53,024
Are you sure?

489
00:29:53,291 --> 00:29:54,692
Hey, Daimon! Don't be silly!

490
00:29:54,893 --> 00:29:56,995
I'll finish this as an assistant.

491
00:29:57,128 --> 00:29:58,963
Who do you think she is?

492
00:29:59,230 --> 00:30:00,765
Do it! It'll be okay.

493
00:30:01,266 --> 00:30:02,600
You never failed.

494
00:30:02,734 --> 00:30:04,002
Dr. Daimon, please.

495
00:30:04,102 --> 00:30:04,936
Move.

496
00:30:05,670 --> 00:30:06,504
Kin.

497
00:30:09,073 --> 00:30:09,941
Yes.

498
00:30:14,345 --> 00:30:15,180
You, too.

499
00:30:15,680 --> 00:30:16,548
What?

500
00:30:25,590 --> 00:30:26,624
Hemostasis.

501
00:30:26,691 --> 00:30:27,792
Bipolar.

502
00:30:28,893 --> 00:30:29,928
They quit.

503
00:30:30,528 --> 00:30:31,763
What's going on?

504
00:30:32,030 --> 00:30:34,499
We have to report to the director.

505
00:30:39,370 --> 00:30:40,371
Inoperable?

506
00:30:40,705 --> 00:30:43,308
Michiko Daimon, stop kidding me!

507
00:30:43,641 --> 00:30:46,244
Why didn't she do her hobby, surgery?

508
00:30:46,377 --> 00:30:49,814
Maybe Daimon tried
to train Morimoto.

509
00:30:49,881 --> 00:30:52,250
Failure teaches
success.

510
00:30:52,517 --> 00:30:54,419
What trains a surgeon?

511
00:30:55,286 --> 00:30:56,120
What?

512
00:30:58,623 --> 00:30:59,891
Reading between the lines.

513
00:31:00,091 --> 00:31:00,959
Yes sir...

514
00:31:01,826 --> 00:31:04,128
Either way the operation failed.

515
00:31:04,863 --> 00:31:07,932
If Chairman Uchikanda
hears about this,

516
00:31:08,433 --> 00:31:09,701
it will be a disaster.

517
00:31:10,802 --> 00:31:11,636
Director.

518
00:31:12,270 --> 00:31:14,539
Let's think about concealing it.

519
00:31:15,740 --> 00:31:16,841
Concealing?

520
00:31:17,141 --> 00:31:18,209
Yes.

521
00:31:18,443 --> 00:31:20,311
- What are you talking about?
- Huh?

522
00:31:20,378 --> 00:31:21,579
Ebina.

523
00:31:23,181 --> 00:31:29,053
The patient asked you to
keep it a secret, right?

524
00:31:29,287 --> 00:31:33,558
Then you kept it.

525
00:31:35,226 --> 00:31:36,194
So...

526
00:31:37,128 --> 00:31:39,230
I don't know anything.

527
00:31:39,364 --> 00:31:40,531
Director.

528
00:31:42,133 --> 00:31:43,201
Read between the lines.

529
00:31:47,338 --> 00:31:48,406
Read between the lines.

530
00:31:49,707 --> 00:31:51,042
- Are you sure?
- Huh?

531
00:31:51,509 --> 00:31:52,377
I...

532
00:31:53,177 --> 00:31:57,548
reported about Chairman Uchikanda's
daughter for you.

533
00:31:59,517 --> 00:32:01,519
- Ebina.
- Yes.

534
00:32:02,253 --> 00:32:03,554
- Ebina.
- Yes.

535
00:32:09,027 --> 00:32:10,228
- Ebina.
- Yes.

536
00:32:11,963 --> 00:32:13,865
- Read between the lines.
- Ahh.

537
00:32:13,932 --> 00:32:17,402
SURGERY DEPARTMENT OFFICE

538
00:32:25,677 --> 00:32:27,478
Why didn't you take my place?

539
00:32:28,046 --> 00:32:28,913
Huh?

540
00:32:29,514 --> 00:32:32,283
I felt good knowing you've
trusted me at first, but

541
00:32:32,717 --> 00:32:35,787
the priority is always
saving the patient, isn't it?

542
00:32:36,187 --> 00:32:38,756
- I know you could have done it.
- No.

543
00:32:39,657 --> 00:32:40,658
What?

544
00:32:41,092 --> 00:32:43,328
Your decision was right.

545
00:32:44,762 --> 00:32:45,630
That's it.

546
00:32:57,342 --> 00:32:58,643
Dr. Morimoto.

547
00:33:01,312 --> 00:33:06,117
We did our best but
we couldn't fully remove it.

548
00:33:09,020 --> 00:33:10,488
But there are other treatments.

549
00:33:10,922 --> 00:33:13,758
Hepatic arterial infusion chemotherapy.
Radiotherapy.

550
00:33:13,825 --> 00:33:14,859
That's enough.

551
00:33:18,296 --> 00:33:21,432
If you couldn't do it,

552
00:33:24,469 --> 00:33:25,903
it cannot be helped.

553
00:33:28,639 --> 00:33:32,243
This is my destiny.

554
00:33:39,584 --> 00:33:40,685
Dr. Morimoto,

555
00:33:44,489 --> 00:33:45,556
I...

556
00:33:49,460 --> 00:33:53,031
can't marry you.

557
00:33:56,367 --> 00:33:58,202
I won't forget the promise.

558
00:33:59,804 --> 00:34:04,509
We promised to get married at
Shirokane Guest House a year from now.

559
00:34:05,610 --> 00:34:07,912
I'll never give up.

560
00:34:13,017 --> 00:34:16,587
No matter what it takes,
I will cure you.

561
00:34:18,322 --> 00:34:21,559
So Shiori,
let's do our best together.

562
00:34:32,637 --> 00:34:33,838
ONE WEEK LATER

563
00:34:44,048 --> 00:34:45,783
What do you mean Shiori will transfer?

564
00:34:46,384 --> 00:34:48,986
I'm sorry but there's
nothing more we can do.

565
00:34:49,053 --> 00:34:50,154
Abandon her?

566
00:34:50,455 --> 00:34:52,824
Before Chairman Uchikanda finds out?

567
00:34:52,957 --> 00:34:54,292
Calm down.

568
00:34:54,425 --> 00:34:56,794
You failed the operation.

569
00:34:57,528 --> 00:34:59,997
The part-timer was also useless.

570
00:35:01,332 --> 00:35:03,434
- A big problem!
- What?

571
00:35:03,634 --> 00:35:05,069
Dr. Daimon started
Shiori's operation.

572
00:35:12,543 --> 00:35:13,544
What's going on?

573
00:35:19,884 --> 00:35:21,152
- Hey, Daimon.
- Move!

574
00:35:21,219 --> 00:35:22,787
What on earth are you thinking?
Stop it!

575
00:35:23,321 --> 00:35:26,390
Hey, Daimon!
Get out of the OR!

576
00:35:27,258 --> 00:35:28,993
Why are you performing
surgery again?

577
00:35:29,227 --> 00:35:30,761
You're bound to fail.

578
00:35:33,865 --> 00:35:36,567
I never fail.

579
00:35:38,469 --> 00:35:39,437
She said it at last!

580
00:35:42,874 --> 00:35:45,543
Yeah! It's bigger!

581
00:35:46,711 --> 00:35:48,012
It was worth waiting a week.

582
00:35:48,613 --> 00:35:49,680
What do you mean?

583
00:35:49,914 --> 00:35:51,249
It has grown big enough.

584
00:35:51,983 --> 00:35:53,384
First, expose the portal vein.

585
00:35:53,518 --> 00:35:54,418
Metzen.

586
00:35:55,920 --> 00:35:57,355
What's going on?

587
00:35:57,922 --> 00:35:59,090
Somebody explain it!

588
00:36:02,827 --> 00:36:03,661
Here is a melon.

589
00:36:04,295 --> 00:36:07,632
I'll explain it.

590
00:36:07,832 --> 00:36:09,233
Why are you here?

591
00:36:10,034 --> 00:36:14,839
If the surgery is successful,
I'll go see the director right away.

592
00:36:15,239 --> 00:36:17,508
She is an important patient.

593
00:36:18,209 --> 00:36:21,879
Daimon chose ALPPS because

594
00:36:22,246 --> 00:36:24,315
she wants to completely cure
her liver cancer.

595
00:36:24,749 --> 00:36:26,817
ALPPS... ALPTIPS.

596
00:36:26,984 --> 00:36:28,786
In this case,

597
00:36:28,853 --> 00:36:34,625
using a usual method, the liver would
be left at less than 20%.

598
00:36:34,825 --> 00:36:37,361
Therefore the liver can't
self-regenerate.

599
00:36:37,628 --> 00:36:40,364
At the first operation,

600
00:36:40,565 --> 00:36:43,634
Daimon ligated
the right portal vein.

601
00:36:44,035 --> 00:36:46,938
To finish up,
you strangulated the blood vessel

602
00:36:47,004 --> 00:36:49,006
to block nutrients and atrophy it

603
00:36:49,273 --> 00:36:53,044
so the left liver enlarges
trying to supplement the right.

604
00:36:53,377 --> 00:36:57,848
But that's the same with
portal vein embolization.

605
00:36:58,382 --> 00:37:03,087
Daimon left the right hepatic artery and
the right hepatic vein.

606
00:37:03,354 --> 00:37:05,723
Split her liver in two.

607
00:37:05,823 --> 00:37:07,625
By inflammatory reaction of
liver transection,

608
00:37:07,692 --> 00:37:09,293
regeneration is accelerated.

609
00:37:10,027 --> 00:37:14,198
It has better regeneration efficiency
than portal vein embolization.

610
00:37:14,632 --> 00:37:18,202
In one week, the residual liver volume
had doubled.

611
00:37:18,336 --> 00:37:19,870
Doubled in size in one week?

612
00:37:20,371 --> 00:37:21,205
Great.

613
00:37:21,339 --> 00:37:26,143
You knew that.
Grandstanding as usual.

614
00:37:26,444 --> 00:37:30,448
To ensure saving more than
20% of the liver

615
00:37:30,648 --> 00:37:32,850
there was no choice.

616
00:37:32,984 --> 00:37:35,586
The inoperable step was
a must anyway.

617
00:37:36,053 --> 00:37:39,724
That's why she let
Morimoto do it.

618
00:37:39,957 --> 00:37:44,528
She wasn't trying to help
Morimoto grow, but the liver.

619
00:37:45,296 --> 00:37:46,230
Liver...

620
00:37:50,334 --> 00:37:52,937
Right hepatic trisegmentectomy
and caudate lobe resection.

621
00:37:53,004 --> 00:37:54,972
Transection of the right hepatic artery
and the right hepatic vein.

622
00:37:55,039 --> 00:37:56,007
3-0 silk.

623
00:37:58,709 --> 00:38:00,978
Dr. Daimon, let me do this.

624
00:38:01,345 --> 00:38:02,780
- No.
- Huh?

625
00:38:02,913 --> 00:38:05,549
You did last time so now it's my turn.

626
00:38:06,651 --> 00:38:08,953
I'm sorry. She's childish.

627
00:38:14,225 --> 00:38:17,695
Dr. Daimon, let me be your assistant.
I'll do anything, even suction.

628
00:38:18,462 --> 00:38:19,530
She is my patient.

629
00:38:23,067 --> 00:38:25,569
Change assistant.
Shape up!

630
00:38:25,903 --> 00:38:26,737
Yes.

631
00:38:27,605 --> 00:38:30,207
First assistant,
ligate the right hepatic artery.

632
00:38:30,308 --> 00:38:31,776
3-0 silk.

633
00:38:55,333 --> 00:38:56,167
Finished.

634
00:38:56,300 --> 00:38:59,870
BP 110 over 82.
Pulse 75, normal sinus rhythm.

635
00:39:00,438 --> 00:39:03,474
Yes! Well done Daimon!

636
00:39:09,547 --> 00:39:11,682
- Thank you.
- Thank you, doctor.

637
00:39:11,816 --> 00:39:14,418
Dr. Daimon,
thank you so much.

638
00:39:22,259 --> 00:39:23,761
- Success?
- Yes.

639
00:39:23,894 --> 00:39:27,064
You mean we saved
Chairman Uchikanda's daughter?

640
00:39:30,000 --> 00:39:31,936
- Excuse me.
- Yes.

641
00:39:33,904 --> 00:39:36,474
So firstly, here is a melon.

642
00:39:36,540 --> 00:39:37,408
So fast this time.

643
00:39:37,475 --> 00:39:39,310
- The bill.
- Bill.

644
00:39:40,745 --> 00:39:41,579
Let me...

645
00:39:41,712 --> 00:39:42,646
$100,000

646
00:39:42,713 --> 00:39:44,315
Oh my God.

647
00:39:46,217 --> 00:39:48,552
This amount is fraud!
Fraud!

648
00:39:48,986 --> 00:39:52,823
It includes hush money,
tuition for Dr. Morimoto.

649
00:39:52,890 --> 00:39:57,428
And fee for reporting to
Chairman Uchikanda.

650
00:39:57,795 --> 00:39:59,063
Considering everything...

651
00:39:59,130 --> 00:40:02,266
the fee is reasonable, indeed.

652
00:40:02,600 --> 00:40:06,837
Now Chairman Uchikanda
owes us much gratitude.

653
00:40:07,171 --> 00:40:10,708
Totei University's future
is bright, thank God.

654
00:40:10,841 --> 00:40:13,043
- Congratulations.
- Yeah.

655
00:40:13,210 --> 00:40:14,645
Totei University Hospital, banzai!

656
00:40:14,712 --> 00:40:19,116
Banza...

657
00:40:19,183 --> 00:40:22,119
Banzai...

658
00:40:22,853 --> 00:40:27,458
To establish a new Faculty of Medicine,

659
00:40:28,025 --> 00:40:30,661
I'd like to propose
the installation of AIs,

660
00:40:31,862 --> 00:40:35,699
artificial intelligence as medical support
at every university hospital in Japan.

661
00:40:38,869 --> 00:40:39,970
What is it?

662
00:40:40,371 --> 00:40:41,472
I'm in the middle of a meeting now.

663
00:40:41,605 --> 00:40:44,275
I'm so sorry. But...

664
00:40:44,975 --> 00:40:48,546
This is an emergency.

665
00:40:48,979 --> 00:40:50,181
I apologize for this.

666
00:40:54,051 --> 00:40:54,885
Chairman.

667
00:40:55,920 --> 00:40:59,723
Please give us a little moment.

668
00:40:59,957 --> 00:41:02,426
May I have a word with you?

669
00:41:03,561 --> 00:41:05,763
Well...

670
00:41:06,630 --> 00:41:08,966
About your daughter,
Shiori Uchikanda.

671
00:41:09,500 --> 00:41:12,136
She had an emergency
hospitalization.

672
00:41:12,503 --> 00:41:18,909
She had liver cancer
and she needed an immediate surgery.

673
00:41:19,009 --> 00:41:21,979
The operation was successful.

674
00:41:23,848 --> 00:41:25,049
What're you talking about?

675
00:41:26,450 --> 00:41:27,284
But...

676
00:41:27,785 --> 00:41:29,720
I mean about your daughter.

677
00:41:29,854 --> 00:41:32,189
I don't have a daughter
named Shiori.

678
00:41:34,124 --> 00:41:37,895
- Huh?
- From my three marriages,

679
00:41:38,863 --> 00:41:40,331
I've only had boys.

680
00:41:43,701 --> 00:41:44,535
Really?

681
00:41:46,871 --> 00:41:48,839
Ah... Ah...

682
00:41:48,906 --> 00:41:50,407
I have hyperpnea.

683
00:41:54,111 --> 00:41:55,346
No, not now.

684
00:41:55,479 --> 00:41:56,580
Hey.

685
00:41:59,783 --> 00:42:01,519
No. Let's leave together.

686
00:42:03,053 --> 00:42:05,322
What does it mean?

687
00:42:06,190 --> 00:42:08,259
I came here for
separate remuneration.

688
00:42:08,893 --> 00:42:11,028
That was close.

689
00:42:11,095 --> 00:42:13,397
Knock on wood...

690
00:42:14,265 --> 00:42:16,400
Glad your surgery
was successful.

691
00:42:16,634 --> 00:42:18,869
That's
really good.

692
00:42:19,703 --> 00:42:21,906
I need to go see your father.

693
00:42:23,207 --> 00:42:27,444
He is the Japan Doctors Club's
chairman. I'm nervous.

694
00:42:32,349 --> 00:42:33,551
Dr. Morimoto.

695
00:42:33,617 --> 00:42:34,451
Yes.

696
00:42:36,820 --> 00:42:40,024
Thank you for curing me.

697
00:42:40,691 --> 00:42:41,625
It's okay.

698
00:42:53,637 --> 00:42:54,505
Here...

699
00:42:56,907 --> 00:42:57,841
I'll give this back.

700
00:42:58,576 --> 00:42:59,410
What?

701
00:42:59,476 --> 00:43:03,781
Are you sure? This is the deposit
for our wedding.

702
00:43:03,914 --> 00:43:04,815
I...

703
00:43:09,219 --> 00:43:10,721
can't marry you.

704
00:43:15,059 --> 00:43:15,893
What?

705
00:43:18,495 --> 00:43:22,299
Please call the police.

706
00:43:26,971 --> 00:43:28,105
Marriage fraud?

707
00:43:28,238 --> 00:43:34,345
She used her surname pretending to be
the chairman's daughter.

708
00:43:34,912 --> 00:43:35,746
And then

709
00:43:37,381 --> 00:43:41,719
she has deceived stupid doctors who are
blinded by the prospect of promotion.

710
00:43:42,786 --> 00:43:43,721
Oh, no.

711
00:43:43,921 --> 00:43:45,389
- Ebina.
- Yes.

712
00:43:45,456 --> 00:43:50,828
I've taught you
how to see through a person.

713
00:43:52,029 --> 00:43:53,130
I'm very sorry.

714
00:43:53,964 --> 00:43:55,733
You couldn't see through?

715
00:43:55,799 --> 00:43:57,434
Are you still alive?

716
00:43:58,936 --> 00:44:01,839
I knew something was not right.

717
00:44:02,606 --> 00:44:04,708
I can't believe it was a fraud.

718
00:44:05,009 --> 00:44:10,848
Dr. Ebina made a hasty conclusion
and we all got caught up with it.

719
00:44:11,982 --> 00:44:15,953
We were desperately trying to
cure a criminal.

720
00:44:17,154 --> 00:44:18,489
The two operations were a total waste.

721
00:44:22,226 --> 00:44:23,060
Sir.

722
00:44:24,161 --> 00:44:26,330
We cured her.
Why say it's a waste?

723
00:44:27,498 --> 00:44:28,499
What?

724
00:44:28,766 --> 00:44:29,633
Because...

725
00:44:30,234 --> 00:44:32,536
Surgeons need to cure whoever
the patient is.

726
00:44:34,838 --> 00:44:35,806
You're right.

727
00:44:35,939 --> 00:44:37,007
What's this?

728
00:44:37,274 --> 00:44:39,610
Too little fried noodles.
Fraud.

729
00:44:39,677 --> 00:44:42,479
Ah! Dr. Morimoto!

730
00:44:42,913 --> 00:44:44,815
There's nothing.
This is fraud.

731
00:44:44,882 --> 00:44:47,151
Don't use the word "fraud" now.

732
00:44:47,885 --> 00:44:49,620
- Have you ever been swindled, Kin?
- I'm not Kin.

733
00:44:51,021 --> 00:44:53,190
See? This is fraud!

734
00:44:53,290 --> 00:44:57,294
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

735
00:44:58,128 --> 00:45:03,434
<i>Her solo weapons are her license and</i>
<i>the skills she has acquired.</i>

736
00:45:05,636 --> 00:45:08,238
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

737
00:45:09,039 --> 00:45:10,040
<i>Also known as...</i>

738
00:45:10,941 --> 00:45:12,609
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

739
00:45:12,676 --> 00:45:13,844
THIS DRAMA IS FICTION

740
00:45:14,378 --> 00:45:15,646
Japanese chess prodigy.

741
00:45:15,713 --> 00:45:16,847
What's wrong with me?

742
00:45:16,914 --> 00:45:18,282
Hippocrates has the answer.

743
00:45:18,348 --> 00:45:20,851
A cutting-edge medical AI.

744
00:45:20,918 --> 00:45:23,053
How can we trust a machine?

745
00:45:23,120 --> 00:45:24,254
Don't underestimate operations.

746
00:45:24,321 --> 00:45:27,257
- We have to examine him further.
- Not necessary.

747
00:45:27,324 --> 00:45:28,692
There it is.
